WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.430
June 1978.

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:06.470
The UK had about 27
million workforce jobs.

3
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.930
About 6.7 million of them
were in manufacturing.

4
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.290
That's a quarter of all jobs.

5
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:17.550
By 2001, its share had almost
halved, to 12.7 per cent.

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.850
Today it's about one in fifteen.

7
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.550
Millions of factory jobs, gone.

8
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.030
So what replaced them?

9
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.870
In this mission, you'll
sort jobs into four sectors:

10
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.550
primary, secondary,
tertiary and quaternary.

11
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.950
Then you'll weigh up
why the shift happened,

12
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.930
from cheaper goods abroad to
machines doing more of the work.

13
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.470
Your mission: find out what
replaced the UK's lost factory jobs.
